From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 22:40:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] Answer the audio/video enable query

RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_AUDIO_VIDEO_ENABLE was declined, which is a reasonable
default only if no client takes the answer seriously. ScummVM does:

    int audio_video_enable = 0;
    environ_cb(RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_AUDIO_VIDEO_ENABLE, &audio_video_enable);
    ...
    if (audio_video_enable & 2)  audio_run();
    if (audio_video_enable & 1)  video_cb(...);

Declining leaves that zero, so ScummVM never submits a frame or an audio
packet. The core loads, detects the game, sizes its framebuffer, sets up its
mixer and runs - and produces a black screen in silence, with nothing logged
anywhere to say why. It looked for a long time like a GLES problem, and the
GLES build was needed too, but this is what actually kept the picture off.

Kodi wants both whenever a game is playing. Run-ahead's suppressed frames are
dropped on the Kodi side instead of here, because a client is entitled to ask
this once and cache it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/src/libretro/LibretroEnvironment.cpp
+++ b/src/libretro/LibretroEnvironment.cpp
@@ -694,11 +694,23 @@
   }
   case RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_AUDIO_VIDEO_ENABLE:
   {
-    retro_av_enable_flags* typedData = static_cast<retro_av_enable_flags*>(data);
-
-    // Not implemented
-    (void)typedData;
-    return false;
+    int* typedData = static_cast<int*>(data);
+    if (typedData != nullptr)
+    {
+      // Answering this is not optional for every client. A core is entitled to
+      // ask whether the frontend currently wants audio and video, and ScummVM
+      // takes the question literally: it initialises the flags to zero, asks,
+      // and then submits a frame only "if (audio_video_enable & 1)" and audio
+      // only "if (& 2)". Declining left it at zero, so it produced no video and
+      // no audio at all - a black screen and silence, with no error anywhere,
+      // for a core that was otherwise running perfectly.
+      //
+      // Kodi always wants both while a game is playing. Run-ahead's suppressed
+      // frames are dropped on Kodi's side rather than here, because this answer
+      // is cached by clients that ask once.
+      *typedData = RETRO_AV_ENABLE_VIDEO | RETRO_AV_ENABLE_AUDIO;
+    }
+    break;
   }
   case RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_GET_MIDI_INTERFACE:
   {
